 Node 20-24, Fastify, TypeScript. WR/SK contracts remain unchanged. Pedia uses
 the concrete two-provider config in `src/psmm.ts`, reused by `src/psmm-diff.ts`.
 2026-10-11 changes are locally mock-tested, not deployed or account-verified.
+
+## WR/SK Write Ambiguity (2026-10-25, agreed with Pages)
+
+A 2xx upstream response that is unreadable / non-JSON on a write endpoint
+(WR `order`, SK `v1/order` AND the actual paid purchase `v1/trx`) means the
+order state is UNKNOWN — it may already have been purchased. The proxy NEVER
+forwards these as HTTP 200 (no fabricated `success:false`), performs NO
+automatic retry, and does NOT cancel an already-forwarded write on client
+disconnect. It returns HTTP 502 with an exact marker that INCLUDES the
+substring `network_error`, so OLD production Pages (which only treats
+`timeout|abort|network|fetch failed|504` as ambiguous) also holds its retry
+fence during rollout, while new Pages matches the marker exactly:
+
+- WR: `502 { success:false, message:"wr_proxy_unreadable_response: network_error" }`
+- SK: `502 { message:"sk_proxy_unreadable_response: network_error" }`
+
+Field shape is kept (WR `success:false`, SK `message`). No new env required.
+Upstream 4xx/5xx still pass through unchanged (business signals read by
+Pages). `PUT` is retained (legacy contract). SK paths are validated after
+normalization (`..` → `400 invalid_sk_path`); body limit uses UTF-8 bytes.
+
+## Egress Proxy (shared agent)
+
+One Undici `ProxyAgent` is created at startup from `QUOTAGUARDSTATIC_URL`
+(`FIXIE_URL` fallback) and REUSED for every request, closed on `app.close()`.
+An invalid configured proxy URL fails closed (startup throw, never silent
+direct fallback). No proxy URL = direct mode (dev only). `SIGTERM`/`SIGINT`
+in the entrypoint await `app.close()` before exit so the shared dispatcher
+actually closes on controlled restart (systemd default would kill Node
+without the `onClose` hook). No per-request agent (socket leak fixed).
+
+## WR/SK Diff Removal Slicing (2026-10-25)
+
+`removed_variant_ids` are sliced independently at ≤200 IDs per request
+(Pages limit; mirrors the SMM 100-slice fix). Only acknowledged slices
+advance the snapshot. A changed WR parent whose lost variant IDs are not yet
+acked RETAINS those IDs in its record (new hash + unacked old IDs, payload
+resent idempotently), so a restart replays only the unacked remainder —
+including lost variants inside a changed parent and fully-vanished parents.
+Newly acked IDs are pruned from ALL retained records on each successful
+slice, so removal-only follow-up batches never resend confirmed IDs forever.
+Covers >200 removals under the <50% missing hold, partial failure, restart,
+and SK removals. No write dedupe by body hash: identical WR bodies can be
+legitimate separate orders.
+
+## Deploy Runbook (VPS)
+
+Ship the WHOLE `dist/` directory (`index.js` + `psmm.js` + `psmm-diff.js` +
+`diff-sync.js` + any new module) — diff/SMM modules are imported at runtime,
+`dist/index.js` alone is NOT enough. Pattern: `npm run build` → backup remote
+`dist/*.bak-*` → `scp dist/*` → `sudo systemctl restart wr-proxy` → check
+`GET /health`; rollback = restore backups + restart. `npm test` uses
+fixtures only (Undici MockAgent, network disabled) + `npx tsc --noEmit`.

